        ("package", "Rebuild the item from the package", '''<ol class="numbered-list"><li><b>Identity</b><p>Product name, type, producer or processor, net contents, jurisdiction, and regulated symbol.</p></li><li><b>Potency basis</b><p>THC and CBD per serving or unit, number of units or servings, package total, and—where relevant—concentration by mass or volume. Keep unlike units separate.</p></li><li><b>Formula</b><p>Active and inactive ingredients, allergens, added cannabinoids, caffeine or other substances, and the intended route.</p></li><li><b>Traceability</b><p>Lot or batch, dates, license identifiers, and an exact-lot report that matches the item rather than a generic certificate.</p></li><li><b>Use and control</b><p>Directions, warnings, child-resistant closure, storage, after-opening rules, expiration, and disposal.</p></li><li><b>Exit</b><p>Seller or manufacturer contact, return terms, recall route, regulator complaint route, and urgent health help.</p></li></ol><p>Photograph the unopened package and receipt when preserving a product problem matters. Do not destroy or discard the identity trail before following a regulator, manufacturer, poison-center, or recall instruction.</p><p><a class="inline-cta" href="../guides/read-a-label/">Open the complete label reconstruction guide <span>→</span></a></p>'''),
