        ("checkout", "Run the ten-gate checkout", '''<ol class="numbered-list"><li><b>Seller:</b><p>The current regulator record matches the business, address, and website.</p></li><li><b>Identity:</b><p>The actual package—not a menu photo—states the exact product and responsible business.</p></li><li><b>Route:</b><p>The label directions define how the product is intended to be used.</p></li><li><b>Math:</b><p>Unit, serving, concentration, and package totals reconcile without mixing incompatible units.</p></li><li><b>Formula:</b><p>Ingredients, allergens, added substances, and route fit the written boundary.</p></li><li><b>Lot:</b><p>The report matches the exact product and lot, and current recalls have been checked.</p></li><li><b>Control:</b><p>The original package, closure, measuring tool, locked storage, and transport plan work at home.</p></li><li><b>Day:</b><p>Driving, work, caregiving, machinery, alcohol, medicines, health questions, and enough time have been addressed before use.</p></li><li><b>Exit:</b><p>Return, complaint, poisoning, emergency, and disposal routes are known.</p></li><li><b>Value:</b><p>The full ownership cost fits the ceiling without turning potency into a quality score.</p></li></ol><p>If the staff member cannot answer, ask whether the label, regulator, processor, or official notice can. “I don't know” is useful. Pressure, certainty without evidence, and an answer that changes with the product being sold are reasons to pause.</p>'''),
