    ("handoff", "Build a one-page source handoff", '''<div class="note-template"><div><span>DECISION</span><i>One question the next person can answer; split health, product, seller, accessory, payment, work, travel, and law</i></div><div><span>OWNER + JURISDICTION</span><i>Agency, service, regulator, court, legislature, employer, clinician, manufacturer; country, state, tribe, property, program, or job</i></div><div><span>SOURCE TYPE</span><i>Statute, regulation, order, license record, recall, reporting portal, official guidance, evidence review, or support service</i></div><div><span>EXACT OBJECT</span><i>Person, product, lot, model, seller, license, address, policy, itinerary, shipment, or claim</i></div><div><span>STATUS + DATES</span><i>Current, archived, proposed, pending, superseded, effective, amended, reviewed, and accessed</i></div><div><span>DIRECT SOURCE</span><i>Official owner, page title, full URL, relevant section, saved copy when appropriate</i></div><div><span>CONCLUSION + LIMIT</span><i>Short paraphrase; what the source establishes, what it does not, and unresolved facts</i></div><div><span>NEXT ROUTE</span><i>Care, complaint, appeal, correction, regulator, counsel, employer process, or dated recheck</i></div></div><p>The handoff is designed to travel: from consumer to clinician, regulator, attorney, employer, manufacturer, poison specialist, or another researcher. Attach only the evidence that route needs. Redact account credentials and unrelated personal information before sharing.</p>'''),
